{
  "case_id": "2017-17-494",
  "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Marty J. Jackley, on behalf of South Dakota (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are two very significant consequences brought about by Quill: First, our states are losing massive sales tax revenues that we need for education, healthcare, and infrastructure. Second, our small businesses on Main Street are being harmed because of the unlevel playing field created by Quill, where out-of-state remote sellers are given a price advantage."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Marty J. Jackley, on behalf of South Dakota (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We would encourage using the doctrines that are already in place with Complete Auto when it comes to a tax assessment to look for discrimination, to look for apportionment issues, to look at that substantial nexus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Malcolm L. Stewart, United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'd like to start by making two brief points about the stare decisis and the wisdom of leaving this matter to Congress. The first point I'd like to make is, whatever this Court decides, whether it overrules Bellas Hess and Quill, whether it leaves those in place, whether it does something in between, Congress can act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Stewart, may -\u00ad may I just ask -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF GEORGE S. ISAACSON ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, by the way, how much does it cost Amazon voluntarily to comply?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Isaacson",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that then\nintroduces the issue of stare decisis, because\nthe standard of stare decisis is that, even\nwhere the Court has ruled incorrectly, there's\na value in settled expectations and standing by\nthe decision previously."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if the Court is\nresponsible for Bellas Hess, and there was from\nthe very beginning strong dissenting opinions,\nand there was a suggestion that there be a test\n-- a test case, why shouldn't the Court take\nresponsibility to keep our case law in tune\nwith the current commercial arrangements? It's\nbeen said that that has been done in the\nantitrust area. Why are we -- Congress -- ask\nCongress to overturn our obsolete precedent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Isaacson",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The notion of software\nbeing a silver bullet, I -- I think, is -- is a\n-- is a real misapprehension. The actual\nlooking up of the rate for the 12,000 different\ntax jurisdictions hardly scratches the surface.\nRetailers need to map their products\nagainst that software, which is rife with\nerrors because common products are defined\ndifferently in different states. And it's not\nmerely the 45 states plus the District of\nColumbia that have sales tax, but there are\nover 500 home rule jurisdictions that have\ntheir own tax bases and definitions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Isaacson",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "70 percent of all small businesses have a\nwebsite. And by the end of 2018, it's\nestimated that 91 percent of small businesses\nwill have a website.\nSo the issue here is not between small\nin-state retailers and out-of-state direct\nmarketers. The real competition is between the\nlarge companies, who are omni-merchants, who\nare multi-channel merchants, who are\nincreasingly dominating the Internet.\nAnd one of the effects, if you\nincrease the cost of admission, if you have\nbarriers to entry, one of the inevitable\neffects is going to be that those small and\nmedium-sized companies are going to be deterred\nand there will be even greater concentration by\nthe largest retailers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-494",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8682f51d917a414d3716e27c7da3187e8d5553648cf28df08163217d5fbf4c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8682f51d917a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
